Contract: `Page` returns at most `limit` items starting at `offset`. If `offset >= len(items)`, it must return an empty slice without panicking. Callers pass non-negative `offset` and `limit`. The implementation is:

```go
func Page(items []string, offset, limit int) []string {
    if limit == 0 {
        return nil
    }
    end := offset + limit
    if end > len(items) {
        end = len(items)
    }
    return items[offset:end]
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
